// 19 — first-class null & the lossless JSON round-trip (spec v0.8.0)
// null is DATA, not a language mechanism: the language itself never produces
// it (absence is {}), it enters only via the null literal or JSON — and it
// leaves through JSON_FORMAT unchanged, so JSON round-trips byte-losslessly.
// Runs identically on the playground, propertee2-java, and propertee-java.

// ── 1. null enters via data: parse an upstream JSON payload losslessly
src = "{\"coupon\":null,\"n\":1,\"tags\":[1,null,3]}"
payload = UNWRAP(JSON_PARSE(src))          // JSON_PARSE returns a Result

PRINT("coupon:", payload.coupon)           // displays as null
PRINT("TYPE_OF:", TYPE_OF(payload.coupon))

// ── 2. null equals ONLY null — {} ("absence") stays a different value
PRINT("== null:", payload.coupon == null)
PRINT("== {}:  ", payload.coupon == {})
PRINT("null == false:", null == false)
PRINT("null == 0:", null == 0)

// ── 3. the round trip is byte-lossless: format(parse(src)) == src
formatted = JSON_FORMAT(payload)
PRINT(formatted)
PRINT("lossless:", formatted == src)

// ── 4. what the language itself NEVER produces: absence is {}, not null
function noop() do
end
PRINT("noop() == {}:", noop() == {})
PRINT("noop() == null:", noop() == null)

// ── 5. check for null explicitly at the data boundary, then branch
function describe_coupon(order) do
    if order.coupon == null then
        return "no coupon (explicit null in the data)"
    end
    return "coupon: " + order.coupon
end
PRINT(describe_coupon(payload))
PRINT(describe_coupon({"coupon": "WELCOME10"}))

// null stays inert data: string + coerces it for display...
PRINT("label: " + null)
// ...but conditions, logic, arithmetic, and member access on null are runtime
// errors — no null propagation. Uncomment to see it fail loudly, with line:col:
// if payload.coupon then PRINT("unreachable") end
